-- title:
--   Maximal orders agree locally at a division place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ and let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $v$-adic completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$ and valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v \subset \mathbb{Q}_v$. Assume that every nonzero element of the $\mathbb{Q}_v$-algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit. Let $\Lambda_1, \Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which are maximal orders in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L63): each $\Lambda_i$ contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, has $\mathbb{Q}$-span equal to all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and every $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda'$ with these four properties and $\Lambda_i \le \Lambda'$ satisfies $\Lambda' = \Lambda_i$. The conclusion is that the two local boxes at $v$ coincide, $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_1\,v = \mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_2\,v$, where $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$ denotes the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c \in \mathcal{O}_v$.
--
--   This is the local uniqueness of maximal orders at a place where the quaternion algebra is a division algebra: both completions are the valuation ring of that division algebra. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset-graph constructions, for instance when comparing level structures and Atkin–Lehner involutions at the ramified prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_localBox_eq_localBox_of_forall_isUnit.lean

